    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0054" n="1110" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p2/pg1110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794.0221/1–2252</note>
                <head>No. 483<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d483-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-01-22">January 22, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum of Telephone
                        Conversations With Mr. Lovett and the President</hi></p>
                <p>I talked with Mr. Lovett about the attached article XV draft. He and General
                    Bradley have approved it. Mr. Lovett authorized me to speak to the President,
                    which I did. The President authorizes us to go ahead.</p>
                <p>The President thought that it might be well for the record, in view of the
                    long-hand letter that he wrote to Bob and the appeal Bob sent him,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d483-f2"/> that I send him a short memorandum attaching this draft,
                    saying that in accordance with the President’s instructions yesterday to Mr.
                    Lovett and me, we have worked out the attached draft, which we believe avoids
                    discrimination against the Japanese on criminal jurisdiction, and we submit it
                    for his approval, and authorization to go ahead with the negotiations. He will
                    approve it, and the record will be straight.</p>
                <p>Either Mr. Rusk or I should tell Mr. Lovett that the President has asked for this
                    brief memorandum.</p>



                <xi:include href="d483-a1.xml" xpointer="d483-a1"/>
            </div>
